  "raw": " usual amount, according to a study by Parental Leave UK.\n\nThe figures follow research that shows lone parents have the most trouble finding paid time off when starting a family due to social attitudes. Forty per cent received employers’ encouragement not to take family time – which could only cause additional stress and anxiety for dads who are often already working hard. Not only must men navigate the privacy issues of responding to the survey, but they also face the stigma associated with taking their few weeks off, if they do at all. It is for this reason that Fatherhood Countdown, an ambition advocacy organisation, has decided to launch Underprivileged Dads, under the Backstage Pass initiative comprising charities such as Baby & Me and Fathers 4 Justice over three years from 2018-2020. Similar organisation, Project Nursery, was launched in 2016 and involved 60 poverty charities sharing confidential dads’ experiences to combat prejudice against dads seeking to address inaccessible services through parental leave.\n\nIn 2017, Ford’s",
